From 1e8cc2a20843e58bcfade07c747ccaa3cf69deab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:23:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ONELIST2, the brain's half: to-dos that ring at their time
 through the brain's own reminder job (plan.u4), the merge, the cap and a late
 offline tick put right, and his bin days read for the Agenda (plan.s10)

A to-do with a day and a time gets one reminder job (marked todo:<id>), so it rings by Web Push with the phone locked; a tick or a
removal cancels it, a new time or day moves it, a repeating one's job repeats with it. mergeTodos keeps the phone's star, day,
repeat and time, keeps two same-words jobs on different days, never doubles; the 300 cap drops the oldest done first and refuses an
add in his words only when all are open; a tick sent late uses the day it was made. The list as read carries the home pack's bin
days (read only).

